// spec: a friend function defined in a class template is instantiated with the instance whose argument argument-dependent lookup finds it through, when it is called ([temp.inst] 11, [basic.lookup.argdep] 4): what its body is no valid code for in that instance is an error, as clang says (a guard for thread A's lazy instance members, D's review of 2026-11-08)
// error: friend_of_an_instance_found_by_adl_is_error.kpp:9: error: a pointer (const char*) does not convert to int32 without a cast
template<typename T>
struct Box
{
  T value{};
  friend int measure(const Box& b)
  {
    T x = "text";
    return 2;
  }
};
int main()
{
  Box<int> b;
  println(measure(b));
  return 0;
}
